Tell the window manager to reload after every save

The dialog writes kwinqtcurverc and then asks the window manager to read that
file again. It sent the request only when the Style group of kwinrc held
kwin3_qtcurve in the key PluginLib. That key and that name belong to the
decoration of the KDE 4 era. The window manager of today writes neither of
them, so the request never left the dialog. The borders of the open windows
kept the old settings until the session restarted.

Send the reloadConfig signal after every save. The window manager reads its
configuration again on that signal, and it then tells each decoration to do
the same. The send is harmless when no window manager listens.

The removed guard read kwinrc alone, so no key of QtCurve changes.

The change sits on the branch work/wm-kcm of the local tree, as commit 2 of 4.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index 351cc609..259fa088 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -1331,15 +1331,8 @@ void QtCurveConfig::save()
         kde.deleteEntry("ButtonLayout");
 
     kwin->save(0L);
-    // If using QtCurve window decoration, get this to update...
-    KConfig kwin("kwinrc", KConfig::CascadeConfig);
-    KConfigGroup style(&kwin, "Style");
-
-    if (style.readEntry("PluginLib", QString()) == "kwin3_qtcurve") {
-        QDBusConnection::sessionBus().send(
-            QDBusMessage::createSignal("/KWin", "org.kde.KWin",
-                                       "reloadConfig"));
-    }
+    QDBusConnection::sessionBus().send(
+        QDBusMessage::createSignal("/KWin", "org.kde.KWin", "reloadConfig"));
 
     // Remove QTCURVE_PREVIEW_CONFIG setting, so that main kcmstyle
     // preview does not revert to default settings!
